
For Task 1, I used Canva to design a one-page infographic that serves as a visual guide for my peers as a Student Digital Ambassador.
The design focuses on three core areas: defining digital literacy as the ability to find and communicate information, highlighting essential tools like GitHub and LinkedIn for professional growth, and outlining safe internet practices such as recognizing phishing and using the 1930 helpline.
I found it particularly interesting to condense complex security and collaboration topics into a single, scannable resource. 
This task helped me realize that digital literacy is a foundational skill for our academic journey at VIT Bhopal, requiring both technical proficiency and responsible online behavior.
